Usage:
  nucleus testserver [flags] <fixture.json>
  nucleus testserver --fixture <fixture.json> [flags]

Load a fixture, then start a server built from configuration only (like serve: your modules are not mounted).

Arguments:
  <fixture.json>  Fixture file loaded before the server starts (alternative to --fixture; not both)

Flags:
  -config string
    	Path to nucleus config file
  -dry-run
    	Run fixture load plan and skip server startup
  -fixture string
    	Path to fixture JSON file
  -force
    	Force destructive actions (recommended in CI)
  -host string
    	Override host
  -port int
    	Override port
  -tables string
    	Comma-separated subset of fixture tables to load
  -truncate
    	Truncate fixture tables before loading (default true)
  -yes
    	Auto-confirm destructive actions without prompt

Examples:
  nucleus testserver --config nucleus.yml fixtures.json
  nucleus testserver --config nucleus.yml --dry-run fixtures.json
